-- title:
--   Faithful flatness of K⊗_{K'}H→ H⊗_{K'}H
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and $H$ a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $k$. Let $K'$ and $K$ be $k$-subalgebras of $H$, together with an algebra structure of $K'$ on $K$ forming a scalar tower $K'\to K\to H$ (so that $K'$ sits inside $K$ compatibly with their inclusions into $H$). Assume that for every $x\in K'$ the comultiplication $\Delta(x)\in H\otimes_k H$ lies in the $k$-span of the elements $a\otimes b$ with $a,b\in K'$, and likewise that for every $x\in K$ the element $\Delta(x)$ lies in the $k$-span of the $a\otimes b$ with $a,b\in K$; assume further that $H$ is flat as a $K'$-module. Let $H_b$ be a commutative ring with a $k$-algebra structure and $\pi\colon H\to H_b$ a surjective $k$-algebra homomorphism whose kernel is the ideal of $H$ generated by $\{x\in K'\;:\;\varepsilon(x)=0\}$, where $\varepsilon$ is the counit, and suppose that $H_b$ is free as a module over the image subalgebra $\pi(K)\subseteq H_b$. Then the ring homomorphism underlying the $K'$-algebra map $K\otimes_{K'}H\to H\otimes_{K'}H$ obtained as the tensor product of the inclusion $K\to H$ with the identity of $H$ is faithfully flat.
--
--   This is the faithful flatness step in Takeuchi's theorem on the correspondence between Hopf ideals and Hopf subalgebras, in the form used in Milne's proof: after the torsor identifications $H\otimes_{K'}H\cong H\otimes_k \pi(H)$ and $K\otimes_{K'}H\cong \pi(K)\otimes_k H$, the displayed map becomes the base change to $H$ of the inclusion $\pi(K)\hookrightarrow H_b$. It is used by [`HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_subalgebra_of_forall_isReduced_of_perfectField`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.faithfullyFlat_subalgebra_of_forall_isReduced_of_perfectField), which deduces faithful flatness of a Hopf algebra over a Hopf subalgebra over a perfect field.
